From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Axboe <axboe@kernel.dk>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 08:12:11 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 58/93] dt-bindings: soc: apple,t6050-sleep: add
 apple,display-method-sleep

The drivers tell one T6050 sleep description from another by the board
or by the node's compatible. What differs for the display coprocessors
is how they take the sleep: through their firmware 27 method table,
with the panel's AV and DP services, or through the sleep's endpoint
transport alone. Say so in the description.

Signed-off-by: Jens Axboe <axboe@kernel.dk>

[re-cut onto the K114s r3d tree]
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/soc/apple/apple,t6050-sleep.yaml  | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/apple/apple,t6050-sleep.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/apple/apple,t6050-sleep.yaml
index c32148802bd..7d26c0049f8 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/apple/apple,t6050-sleep.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/soc/apple/apple,t6050-sleep.yaml
@@ -144,6 +144,14 @@ properties:
       The GFX die's wake sources left enabled for a sleep. From the ADT, set by
       the bootloader.
 
+  apple,display-method-sleep:
+    type: boolean
+    description: |
+      The display coprocessors take the sleep through their firmware 27 method
+      table: its sleep call and its swap, the panel's AV and DP services and the
+      external processors' handling around a sleep. Without it they keep the
+      method table they had and take the sleep's endpoint transport alone.
+
   apple,clk-gating-boot:
     $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32-matrix
     items:
